{{- /*
plugin_page.gohtml is the shell of a screen a PLUGIN registered (ADR 0155).

It is the second page of ADR 0030's shape and it is deliberately the same shape
as the first (reviews.gohtml): the server renders a shell, a script fills it from
/admin/v1 with the operator's own session. The difference is only where the script
came from — a plugin registered its BYTES and the panel serves them from its own
origin, which is what lets the content policy stay script-src 'self'.

A plugin ships no template and never will. ADR 0030 refused server-renderer
extension points because they put every plugin's markup in this binary, and this
page is what replaces that: one shell, owned here, for every registered screen.

The noscript block is not a courtesy. A page whose whole content arrives by
script shows an empty box when the script fails, and an operator cannot tell that
from "there is no data".
*/ -}}
{{ define "body" }}
<h1>{{ .Title }}</h1>

<noscript>
  <p class="notice">This screen is a client of the admin API and needs JavaScript.</p>
</noscript>

<div id="plugin-page" data-api="{{ .APIPrefix }}">
  <p class="notice">Loading…</p>
</div>

<script src="{{ .PageScript }}" defer></script>
{{ end }}
